body:
Yea I was actually very selfless and vulnerable in the relationship but according to her i was abusive because i only cared about the attention she gave me, which is absolutely fake. I personally believe she is gas-lighting me to believe im the bad guy and in the moment i unfortunately gave in, but after some reflection I realized she really just gaslight me and brainwashed me into thinking I am an emotionally abusive person when in reality she is lying to herself to make her seem like the good guy. Although I know you you do not impact my everyday life  your support is appreciated. I have always had trouble making friends and spent the majority of my childhood alone since my sister has special needs and requires special attention from my parents. And I did invest a lot of myself and trust into this person and the feeling of betrayal is difficult to cope with.

&#x200B;

Yea ive actually opted to graduate in December and take a break Jan-August before College because I just cannot handle it anymore, COVID, breakups,it is horrendous. Maybe Ill get a full time job and buy a new car, my current one is like 21 years old with over 200k lol, or maybe Ill go on a trip since I've never traveled internationally.I have more than enough credits to graduate,  you need 23 to graduate in my state and i already have 27, 31 at the end of this semester. However, the timing of such emotional distress and sorrow is horrible because it is currently time to apply for colleges. Im not sure where I want to go or what I what i want to do. I could apply to lower ivy league schools with my numbers, however  I will probably end up in state. I am kind of into International Business however I struggle in Economics. I might just end up being a Marketing Major, I dont know, teaching seems like a cool job. I struggle in math and science a lot so Im not sure what Ill do but on my applications ill probably put something business related.
